# A 1 x 1 m portal on Baldor ironless linear motors (docs/baldor_linear.md):
# a bridge on two Y rails 1.2 m apart, each side an LMCF08F (1152 N peak),
# a carriage with an LMCF08E (753 N peak) on the bridge, a tool head (Z
# axis, spindle) on the carriage. 1 um absolute scales. The frame (welded
# steel, 600 kg) stands on rubber leveling feet. Masses, modes and
# friction are GUESSES of a light laser / router portal.
drive y1 y.conf sim.txt 60.96
drive y2 y.conf sim.txt 60.96
drive x x.conf sim.txt 60.96
# machine X, Y [mm] of the frame's centre, the end stops
origin 500 500
stroke -5 1005 -5 1005
# frame: M [kg] J [kg m^2], feet modes x y yaw [Hz], damping ratio
frame 600 200 12 10 14 0.05
rails 1.2
# moving masses [kg], yaw inertias [kg m^2]; the coils included
bridge 30 3.6
carriage 5 0.02
# the guide blocks resist the bridge's yaw (racking) [Nm/rad], damping ratio
racking 2e5 0.02
# head: M J, modes x / y at the rails / y at mid-span [Hz], damping ratio
head 7 0.02 45 55 28 0.03
# guides: Coulomb [N] (each Y side), viscous [N s/m]; cable chains included
guidey 25 30
guidex 15 15
# the DC bus: 230 V mains through a diode bridge (1 ohm), no capacitors in
# the supply, only the three drives' own (470 uF each); no brake chopper
bus 1410 230 1.0
home 500 500
